<Group view="presentation" hide-input="false" hide-output="true" inline-output="false" labelreference="L176" drawlabel="true">
<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Title" alignment="left">|<Font encoding="UTF-8">\317\204| &lt; \316\273</Font> .  Since                     a+d = <Font encoding="UTF-8">\316\273+\317\204  and  ad-bc = \316\273\317\204 ,                                 (1)there are 2 free nonnegative parameters  a  and  b  (say).  Note  (a,c)  is  the </Font>image of  (1,0) .Solving for  d  and  c  gives                                 d  =  <Font encoding="UTF-8">(\316\273 + \317\204) - a                                                     (2)                               bc  = (a - \317\204) \303\227(\316\273 - a)                                              (3)It is necessary and sufficient that  a  be chosen so      a \342\210\210 [ \317\204 , \316\273 ]  in case  \317\204 \342\211\245 0 ,  and a \342\210\210 [ 0 , \316\273 -  |\317\204| ]  in case  \317\204 \342\211\244 0 .   (4)</Font>(in either case this is an interval of length  <Font encoding="UTF-8">\316\273 -  |\317\204|. ) The first restriction is necessary since  bc \342\211\245 0 .   The second is necessary since  d\342\211\2450 . They are also sufficient, since if they are satified then both </Font> d and bc  are  nonnegative and so  c  and  d  can be chosen to be nonnegative.<Font italic="true">Input Summary</Font>:In the program,  choose  <Font encoding="UTF-8">\316\273</Font> (i.e. lam) &gt; 0,   then  |<Font encoding="UTF-8">\317\204 (i.e. tau)| &lt; \316\273 ,  then </Font> a  as in (4) above, then  any nonnegative  b .Alternatively: First choose  <Font encoding="UTF-8">\316\273  , then   a  such that  0 \342\211\244 a &lt; \316\273, then  \317\204  so (4) is satisfied, then </Font>any nonnegative  b .</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
